A||||2||MikeyJP||Fading Finish - Hood Only!
Z||000000||MikeyJP||09-05-99||10:27 AM||||I have a red '86 SE that has always been garage kept or covered.  All the paint is cherry, except I have been noticing the last six months the front hood is loosing its luster, fading and seems to be oxidizing. It is factory, based on the stickers (I bought it in '88). No other parts of the paint are following or loosing any luster at all. But, on the hood - it is startlingly obvious. I have always used reccomended products on the finish, and wash it too regularly. Now, I am afraid to take a strong compound product to the plastic. Am I worng? Help. Any ideas or suggestions short of new paint??? Mike P.
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||12:31 PM||||what you are descibing sounds like clear coat failure. Not much you can do about it. You could try carefully compounding it but don't hope for miracles.
Z||000002||Cooter||09-05-99||04:03 PM||||You could find some one to re-clear the hood for you. It is such a small job that many shops won't do it because they won't make much money from it. The materials will not cost much- all you should need would be a quart of clear and depending on which brand of paint you use, a half pint of hardener or a half pint of hardener and a half pint of reducer. If the paint is really oxidized, you might need a pint of basecoat and some basecoat reducer. It could be done in about 1.5 - 2 days, depending on the weather.
